<div class="postcell post-layout--right">

    <span class="d-none">$\begingroup$</span>
    <div class="s-prose js-post-body" itemprop="text">
                
<p>Fix integers <span class="math-container">$n\ge 3,d\ge 2$</span>, and partitions <span class="math-container">$\lambda_1,\ldots,\lambda_n$</span> of <span class="math-container">$d$</span>. Let <span class="math-container">$\mathcal{H}$</span> be the moduli space of degree <span class="math-container">$d$</span> covers <span class="math-container">$f:C\to\mathbb{P}^1$</span> that have ramification profiles <span class="math-container">$\lambda_i$</span> over pairwise distinct marked points <span class="math-container">$x_i\in\mathbb{P}^1$</span>, where <span class="math-container">$C$</span> is smooth and projective and the <span class="math-container">$x_i$</span> form the set of all branch points of <span class="math-container">$f$</span>. I believe it is true <span class="math-container">$\mathcal{H}$</span> is étale over <span class="math-container">$M_{0,n}$</span>, and in particular smooth. Can someone point me to a reference for this fact? I know where to look in the case of simple ramification, <span class="math-container">$\lambda_i=(2,1,1\ldots,1)$</span>, for instance <a href="https://perso.univ-rennes1.fr/matthieu.romagny/articles/hurwitz_spaces.pdf" rel="noreferrer">https://perso.univ-rennes1.fr/matthieu.romagny/articles/hurwitz_spaces.pdf</a> and the references therein, but not in general. </p>
    </div>

